<title>GREECE: GREEK 1MTH ATHIBOR JUMPS TO 11.50PCT ON FX OUTFLOWS.</title>
<headline>GREEK 1MTH ATHIBOR JUMPS TO 11.50PCT ON FX OUTFLOWS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek one-month Athibor, the reference rate for the local interbank market, soared to 11.50 percent from Wednesday's 10.93 percent on continued forex outflows, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Interest rates have jumped, trading in the 11.50-11.80 percent bands and bid-ask spreads have widened,&quot; a senior dealer at a foreign bank said. &quot;It definitely relates to ecu and mark buying for drachmas.&quot;</p>
<p>Dealers said the market was nervous and interest rates could go higher if forex outflows continued.</p>
<p>There were unconfirmed reports from London on Wednesday evening that U.S. hedge funds were requesting information about the central bank's forex reserves, dealers said.  </p>
<p>Money market dealers said the central bank should engage in</p>
<p>more complex money and forex operations to inject liquidity into</p>
<p>the interbank money market and support the drachma by selling</p>
<p>foreign currencies intraday or at the fixing.</p>
<p>The bid rate (Athibid) soared to 10.84 percent from 10.43</p>
<p>percent.</p>
